# Scripts in package.json that no workflow runs, and why.
#
# `npm run spine --parity` requires every script to be either RUN BY A WORKFLOW
# or listed here with a reason. It is a list of exceptions rather than a pattern
# because the honest reasons have nothing in common — a generator, a renderer, a
# server and a deliberately-manual audit are four different arguments, and a
# regex over the names would have to guess which one applies.
#
# A new script defaults to FAILING this. That is the point: a gate that nobody
# wired into CI looks exactly like a gate that is running, from every angle
# except this one.
#
# One per line: name — reason.

branch:state — deliberately NOT a Spine step. On a runner at a promote, origin/main is already the merge being pushed, so it is red by construction. It runs as a commit guard via .branch-guard instead.
gates:audit — plants a defect per gate and restores; minutes long and it MUTATES the tree. Run by hand when adopting or changing a gate, never on a push.
prepare — an npm lifecycle hook that installs the commit guard into .git/hooks. Nothing for CI to assert: actions/checkout leaves .git/hooks empty by definition, which is why the workflow runs branch-guard with --artefact instead.

# Generators. The `:check` beside each one is the gate, and IT is in CI; running
# the generator there would WRITE the file whose drift the gate exists to find.
brand — generated by brand:check's counterpart; brand:check is the gate.
changelog — writes CHANGELOG.md from src/ui/changelog.ts; changelog:check is the gate.
manual — writes public/manual.html from the doc; manual:check is the gate.
thesis — writes public/why.html from the doc; thesis:check is the gate.

# Renderers. These ASSERT NOTHING by design — they take the screen as a person
# meets it and write it to a file, because the missing step was never a check.
look — the app at 390x844, for looking at.
import:look — the other-planner import with a file chosen, for looking at.
serve — a static server the walks use; not a check.

# Covered by a fuller command that IS in CI.
editions:check — a check-only subset of build:sync, which the Spine runs as "Two editions".
quotes:check — a local wrapper for the hub's quote-check; CI runs the canonical copy out of .hub-gates.
test — `npm run typecheck && npm run test:only`, and the Spine runs both halves as their own steps so a type error and a failing test are told apart in the log.
